# Query Language: Syntax Reference

Spec: QuerySyntax
Purpose:
  Define the formal syntax of the SDD query language.

Owns: queries/syntax.sdd

TokenReference:
  @<concept_name>
    Resolves canonical concept and all related knowledge:
      concept → skills → tasks → architecture → decisions → tests → failures → proofs

  @<type>:<state>
    Type-filtered queries:
      @task:open        — tasks with execution state PENDING or READY
      @task:running     — tasks currently executing
      @task:blocked     — tasks blocked by dependencies
      @task:review      — tasks awaiting review
      @task:failed      — tasks that have failed
      @task:completed   — tasks that are done
      @skill:active     — skills in ACTIVE status
      @skill:dormant    — skills not currently referenced
      @decision:approved — decisions in APPROVED state
      @decision:challenged — decisions under challenge
      @proof:verified   — proofs that passed verification
      @proof:pending    — proofs awaiting verification

  @impact:<concept>
    Blast radius query — what is affected if this concept changes?

  @unknown:<scope>
    @unknown:blocking   — unknowns blocking active tasks
    @unknown:unresolved — all unresolved unknowns
    @unknown:all        — all registered unknowns

  @risk:<level>
    @risk:low
    @risk:medium
    @risk:high
    @risk:critical

  @domain:<name>
    Scope-limited queries to a specific domain

  @why:<task> uses <skill>
    Why-chain query — trace reasoning chain

RelationshipNavigation:
  @task.T2041 → uses → @skill.idempotency
  @decision.D88 → selects → @architecture.ddd
  @concept.transaction → defined_by → @reference.R12

State: +
